{
  "title": "Work Health and Safety (General) Regulations 2022",
  "abstract": "The Work Health and Safety (General) Regulations 2022 provides comprehensive regulatory framework supporting the WHS Act 2020 in Western Australia. These regulations establish detailed requirements for managing workplace health and safety risks across various hazardous work activities including confined spaces, falls prevention, and high risk work licensing. The regulations prescribe specific control measures following the hierarchy of controls, exposure standards for noise and hazardous substances, and administrative requirements such as permits and licenses. Key provisions address plant and structures safety, hazardous chemicals management, construction work requirements, and demolition procedures. This legislative instrument ensures duty holders implement systematic approaches to risk management with clear compliance obligations and enforcement mechanisms.",
